## Selection rule

Adopted framing: conception/jetp-short-paper-framing-2026-09-15.md.
Develop three dimensions on the frozen 0730 snapshot: A progression by transition
function, B public/private financing and instruments, C pre/post-JETP operation
history. Develop each candidate result thoroughly, then choose a dominant finding
illuminated by the other two panels. For each, document its intrinsic research
interest, the evidence and definition coverage supporting it, sensitivity to
reasonable accounting/date/perimeter choices, and what published literature it
extends, contradicts or leaves open. Search the published literature before
selection; a familiar descriptive statistic is not a contribution by itself.
Rank the three using those four criteria and retain the ranking, rejected
candidates and contrary evidence. Astra independently reviews the ranking before
the author selects one central result.

## First test

A null or mixed fixture with missing data must render legibly, show coverage, and contain no causal vocabulary. The graphic is reproducible from its run manifest and data extract.

## Actions and exit criteria

Develop and compare three result candidates before selection. Select one
result sentence supported by 0730's pre-specified statistics; render one central
figure with three coordinated panels on the same operations. Show common-sample
coverage, unknowns and exclusions; if different samples are needed, label them and
restrict joint interpretations. Keep financial status and physical implementation
distinct. Deliver caption,
plotted data, hashes and sensitivity references. Astra performs an independent
scientific review focused on claim/figure alignment and candidate ranking.

- [ ] Three substantively distinct candidate results assessed against published literature
- [ ] Candidate ranking records intrinsic interest, robustness, coverage and contrary evidence
- [ ] Author selects the central result after Astra's independent review
- [ ] Selected figure and claim reproduce from the frozen run and preserve non-causal language

